Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Thirteenth Challenge/Solution pair. Proves, for every dimension N, g ≥ 0, L,
cap function C and coordinate a, that ∫_{T̃} (L − Σx)^p x_a^e equals the
closed form of Proposition 10.2 (integral_supportT): pointwise stratification
and inclusion–exclusion, translation with null faces, two-group Dirichlet
integrals from V1 by Fubini, and binomial counting; boundary cases R = ∅,
R = univ, N = 0 and empty index types. At Table 3 the entry
I_T[(1,∅),(0,(2))] = ∫ (L − P₁)P₂ = gramEntryQ (gram_entry_integral,
gram_entry_B21 in V0's generators), with the rational value kernel-checked
row by row (Solution/GramEntryCert.lean) and equal to V2a's exploratory
value. Comparator suite gram_entry_v2b added (13 suites); controls and
result record included. Axioms: propext, Quot.sound, Classical.choice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
